	2	Full Backup!
					Definition:
					A Full Backup copies all data in the database, regardless of previous backups.
					Every backup contains the complete database.
		Advantages
					Fastest restore.
					Easy to manage.
					Only one backup is needed to restore.
		Disadvantages
					Takes the most storage.
					Backup takes longer.

	3	Differential Backup
					A Differential Backup stores all changes since the last Full Backup.
		Advantages
					Faster restore than incremental.
					Easier management.
		Disadvantages
					Differential backups grow larger each day.
	4	Incremental Backup
					An Incremental Backup stores only changes since the previous backup (whether full or incremental).
		Advantages
					Smallest backup size.
					Fastest backup operation.
					Saves storage space.
		Disadvantages
				Restore is slower because all incremental backups must be applied in sequence.
	
